class Solution {

    public static ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> findPairsWithGivenSum(int target, Node head) {

        ArrayList<ArrayList<Integer>> ans = new ArrayList<>(); // Stores all valid pairs.

        if (head == null) return ans; // Empty DLL, so no pairs.

        Node left = head; // Left pointer starts from the first node.
        Node right = head; // Used to reach the last node.

        while (right.next != null) { // Move right pointer to the last node.
            right = right.next;
        }

        while (left != right && left.prev != right) { // Continue until pointers meet or cross.

            int sum = left.data + right.data; // Calculate the current pair sum.

            if (sum == target) { // Pair found.

                ArrayList<Integer> pair = new ArrayList<>(); // Store one valid pair.
                pair.add(left.data); // Add left value.
                pair.add(right.data); // Add right value.

                ans.add(pair); // Add the pair to the answer.

                left = left.next; // Move left forward.
                right = right.prev; // Move right backward.
            }

            else if (sum < target) {
                left = left.next; // Sum is smaller, so move left to increase the sum.
            }

            else {
                right = right.prev; // Sum is larger, so move right to decrease the sum.
            }
        }

        return ans; // Return all pairs.
    }
}
Complexity:
Time Complexity: O(n)
    Finding the last node takes -O(n).
    The two pointers together traverse the DLL only once, so the total remains O(n).
Auxiliary Space: O(1)
    Only left, right, and a few variables are used. The output list is not counted.
Total Space: O(k) ,where k is the number of pairs stored in the answer.
